  "description": "Authored profile cross-product scenario through the owned C06 route over real admission and storage. Each query is run under each exact PromQL profile with the declared enabled gates (resolved to a registered feature set), and every profile carries its OWN expectation: a function added in 3.13.5 is a language error under 3.1.0 and a value under 3.13.5, while an unchanged selector is the same value under both. The cross product is run hot, after a flush, after a compaction and after a restart. Expectations are authored from the fixture and the version-difference ledger, never observed from an upstream engine. Native integer and float histograms (a count above 2^53, a counter reset, custom buckets) and LogQL logs under the pinned Loki profile are run through the same four stages: the integer histogram's count 2^54+1 converts to the nearest even float64 (2^54), a fall of the count is one counter reset, and a custom-bucket histogram answers its authored count; the LogQL count is the number of admitted lines.",
  "runner": {
    "command": "soundpost-querycheck smoke",
    "storage": "real",
    "control": "real",
    "http": "own",
    "modes": [
      "single"
    ],
    "stages": [
      "hot",
      "flush",
      "compaction",
      "restart"
    ]
  },
  "fixture": {
    "projects": [
      "project-a"
    ],
    "sources": [
      {
        "id": "source-a",
